{"uid":"62aacbfdedffc0b6","name":"test_no_stale_parked_panel_after_a_commit_scan_hold_following_an_answered_gate","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_parked#test_no_stale_parked_panel_after_a_commit_scan_hold_following_an_answered_gate","historyId":"8729be9f0fee14bf248bfb1ea2d0392f","time":{"start":1791930235855,"stop":1791930250364,"duration":14509},"description":"Cure task cure-01-02-4 (PRD B.1, D.1; DoD 2/4): a task-boundary\n    commit-secret-scan hold reuses the SAME `operator_input_needed` reason\n    string an already-answered review gate left behind, but emits no fresh\n    `operator_escalation` event of its own\n    (`LoopSupervisor._pause_for_commit_secret_hit`). The panel must not\n    resurrect that answered gate's own stale question/finding list -- and a\n    genuinely new review escalation raised once that hold is answered still\n    appears, with its OWN findings and consequences, not the stale ones.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Cure task cure-01-02-4 (PRD B.1, D.1; DoD 2/4): a task-boundary<br />\ncommit-secret-scan hold reuses the SAME <code>operator_input_needed</code> reason<br />\nstring an already-answered review gate left behind, but emits no fresh<br />\n<code>operator_escalation</code> event of its own<br />\n(<code>LoopSupervisor._pause_for_commit_secret_hit</code>). The panel must not<br />\nresurrect that answered gate's own stale question/finding list -- and a<br />\ngenuinely new review escalation raised once that hold is answered still<br />\nappears, with its OWN findings and consequences, not the stale ones.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791929070280,"stop":1791929070280,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factor